    "customfield_12311020": null,
    "customfield_12313320": "<div style='font-weight:bold;color:red;text-align:center'>This project has a <a href=\"https://lucene.apache.org/core/discussion.html\">user mailing list and an IRC channel</a> for support. If you are looking for support, or if you are not sure whether the behavior that you are observing is expected or not, please discuss it there first.</div>",
    "customfield_12314134": null,
    "duedate": null,
    "customfield_12314132": null,
    "customfield_12314131": null,
    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12425853/comment/12710836",
          "id": "12710836",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=earwin",
            "name": "earwin",
            "key": "earwin",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Earwin Burrfoot",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "If you reopen() MSR with unchanged segments, the resulting MSR will share SR instances for these segments.\nConsequently, when you delete a doc in one of said segments through new MSR, deletion will be visible in original MSR, as no checks for shared SRs are done in delete().\n\nThe patch illustrates the bug by altering existing test to reopen MSR->MSR instead of SR->MSR.\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=earwin",
            "name": "earwin",
            "key": "earwin",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Earwin Burrfoot",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2009-05-19T19:19:50.228+0000",
          "updated": "2009-05-19T19:19:50.228+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12425853/comment/12710872",
          "id": "12710872",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Good catch!\n\nSo we are missing a clone() on the old subreaders, when referencing them from the new MultiSegmentReader?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2009-05-19T20:39:10.633+0000",
          "updated": "2009-05-19T20:39:10.633+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12425853/comment/12710894",
          "id": "12710894",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=earwin",
            "name": "earwin",
            "key": "earwin",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Earwin Burrfoot",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Either that. Or having boolean readerShared[] as a property of MSR, and check it on each modification attempt -> lazy clone().\n\n*rant on*\nOr make readers immutable :) I already have a patch that removes norm updates, lazy loading and synchronization. Then we only need to do deletes in IndexWriter without resorting to its reader pool.\nBy the way, do we need public IR cloneability? Not for Lucene internals, but for actual users? That really looks like one more feature that can be safely removed.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=earwin",
            "name": "earwin",
            "key": "earwin",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Earwin Burrfoot",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2009-05-19T21:46:04.140+0000",
          "updated": "2009-05-19T21:46:04.140+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12425853/comment/12711006",
          "id": "12711006",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=earwin",
            "name": "earwin",
            "key": "earwin",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Earwin Burrfoot",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Lazy clone() is a bad idea, since it has to be synced.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=earwin",
            "name": "earwin",
            "key": "earwin",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Earwin Burrfoot",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2009-05-20T05:01:09.602+0000",
          "updated": "2009-05-20T05:01:09.602+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12425853/comment/12711086",
          "id": "12711086",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "bq. Lazy clone() is a bad idea, since it has to be synced.\n\nRight; I think we should simply clone shared subreaders on reopen.\n\nbq. Or make readers immutable\n\nI think it's too soon to do this.  In theory, NRT should enable us to deprecate deletions from IW, but 1) we need NRT released and some real experience before doing so, and 2) we still need to get setNorm working from IW.\n\nbq. By the way, do we need public IR cloneability?\n\nI think we do?  Eg it enables you to clone a readOnly reader to a read/write one in order to do deletes/setNorm.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mikemccand",
            "name": "mikemccand",
            "key": "mikemccand",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael McCandless",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
